<tr><td>What is CME?</td><td>Runtime exception when collection structurally modified during iteration (outside iterator&#x27;s remove)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Do concurrent collections throw CME?</td><td>No — never</td></tr>
<tr><td>When must you use concurrent collections?</td><td>Scalable multi-threaded applications (many threads, shared data)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Name three concurrent collection classes</td><td>ConcurrentHashMap, CopyOnWriteArrayList, CopyOnWriteArraySet</td></tr>
<tr><td>Why CopyOnWrite instead of ConcurrentList?</td><td>Behavior is copy-on-write — explained in detail in CopyOnWriteArrayList lecture</td></tr>
</table>
